    "Pet Insurance",
    "PawSquad",
    "As a pet insurance customer with us, you have access to PawSquad whenever you're worried about your pet's health.",
    "PawSquad is an online vet advice service. It gives you access to qualified UK-registered vets 24 hours a day all year round for advice and treatment options.",
    "That means if you’re worried about your pet’s health, you’ve got a vet at your fingertips to support you. You can chat to them over the phone, text or video – whatever's best for you.",
    "All our levels of pet insurance include access to PawSquad.",
    "Here's what you can expect from PawSquad:",
    "Has your pet got tummy troubles? A cough that won't go away?",
    "These consultations are for you to chat through any health concerns you might have about your pet.",
    "You can get vet advice 24 hours a day, all year round. That means even if it’s 2am when you’re worried about your pet’s health, you've got someone to turn to.",
    "All of the vets are registered with the Royal College of Veterinary Surgeons and have at least five years of clinical experience.",
    "You can chat to the vet however you want – whether that’s over the phone, a video call or sending them a chat message.",
    "It’s whatever is the most comfortable and convenient for you!",
    "PawSquad is there to offer you advice and treatment recommendations when you need it.",
    "They can help with different worries and mishaps, including:",
    "vomiting or diarrhoea",
    "eye and ear problems",
    "coughing and sneezing",
    "itching and skin problems",
    "minor injuries and accidents",
    "They can help you decide whether you need to see a vet in person.",
    "Remember, if your pet needs urgent medical care or has had a serious accident, head to your nearest vet surgery right away.",
    "If you have pet insurance with us, you have access to PawSquad - it's that simple. All you need to do is sign up using the same email address that's registered to your Admiral pet policy.",
    "Visit PawSquad’s website to sign up.",
    "Enter your details and some info about your pet.",
    "This is how they check if you have access to their services.",
    "So, you're all set up with your pet insurance and your PawSquad account. Here's what to do next if you're worried about your pet's health.",
    "Log in to the PawSquad app on your phone or through their website.",
    "If you’re on a Multi Pet policy, tick which one of your pets you’re worried about.",
    "Choose the 24/7 vet service – this is free to access with your policy.",
    "You can either choose to be connected to a vet there and then, or book a time slot later that works for you.",
    "You'll get a detailed report afterwards, with everything you spoke about and the vet's advice. You can share this report with your registered vet if you'd like.",
    "Head to our cat or dog insurance pages to find out more about what our pet insurance includes.",
    "Still have questions about PawSquad and how it works? We've got you.",
